\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces SoloParkour leverages a two-stage RL approach to train visual locomotion policies in simulation. Stage 1: we train a privileged policy that observes a heightmap scan of its surroundings and the height of the nearby floating objects using PPO with Constraints as Terminations (CaT)~\citep  {chane2024cat}. Stage 2: we train a policy from depth pixels using a variant of DDPG with CaT that learns from a dataset of privileged experience collected using the Stage 1 policy. }}{5}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method}{{3}{5}{SoloParkour leverages a two-stage RL approach to train visual locomotion policies in simulation. Stage 1: we train a privileged policy that observes a heightmap scan of its surroundings and the height of the nearby floating objects using PPO with Constraints as Terminations (CaT)~\citep {chane2024cat}. Stage 2: we train a policy from depth pixels using a variant of DDPG with CaT that learns from a dataset of privileged experience collected using the Stage 1 policy}{figure.caption.12}{}}
